  "name": "website-launch-check",
  "description": "Launch readiness check for a site built with this toolkit: runs the site's own build and tests first, then checks only what they cannot (legal pages, E-E-A-T and local signals, content the site's settings call for, testimonial consent, what only a deployed site shows, the Cloudflare zone settings the owner reads in the dashboard), asks only where the owner's intent decides, and writes a dated report with a verdict to docs/launch/ as Markdown plus a self-contained HTML page. When the site replaces an older one, also a current-vs-new comparison with a redirect map for every old address. Runs three times in new-website (baseline after the scaffold, the verdict before launch, the live re-check once launch day's work is done) and on its own. Trigger phrases: \"launch check\", \"ready to launch\", \"what's missing before launch\", \"pre-launch\", \"go live\", \"launch audit\", \"relaunch\", \"compare the old and the new site\", \"post-launch gap analysis\".",
